{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::execute` receives a context for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node` and computes its\ncompleted answer:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse std::future::Future;\n\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Select inputs through cx and compute the completed answer.\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        cx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nAn `Ok` value is the answer defined by\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.answer`.\nAn `Err` value reports a [validation error](running-criteria.md#habeas-req-requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.ValidationError).",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I did not read the implementation source. I judged the tests from the supplied inputs. `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute` has three obligations. Each one is covered by a test marked `{test}` for it.\n\n**1. `execute` receives a context for the criterion's source node, and tracked reads go through it.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs `Review` for `Node(1)`. It asserts that the saved dependency is `Dependency::Node(Node(1), fingerprint \"ordinary computation\")`. That shows the context was bound to the source node and recorded the read.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` has `execute` call the context, including an `ask` callback. It asserts the dependency `Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"root\"))` and that the intermediate request \"Check intermediate result 7\" is made.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` runs the future through a `Send`-requiring helper. It checks outputs of 17 and 23, a single execution, and that the stored evidence round-trips.\n\n**2. An `Ok` value is the completed answer, including a negative one.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` makes `ParseAnswer` return `false`. It asserts that `verify` returns `Ok`, that `answer.output()` is false, that the dependency is recorded, and that the stored output is `json!(false)`.\n- The `agent/tests.rs` test above asserts `!result.output().result` with its rationale. That is another negative completed answer returned as `Ok`.\n\n**3. An `Err` value reports a validation error.**\n- `ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured` is asserted in both the `agent/tests.rs` test and the runner test. In the runner test, nothing is stored and no reads are recorded.\n- `ValidationError::Graph(\"missing\")` is asserted in `fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]`. It comes from a read inside the callback. That test also checks that no evidence record is written.\n- `ValidationError::Agent(_)` is asserted in `fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]`. It covers both `ctx.ask` and `verify_with_agent`, and asserts that no records are stored.\n- `ValidationError::Output(error)` with `is_syntax()` is asserted in `fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` for the input \"not JSON\". It also asserts that no records are stored.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks the `Agent` payload and its display text.\n\nThe tests assert outcomes, not just execution. They cover both the success and error halves of the `Result` signature. They also separate a negative answer from an error. I found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept. There are no acknowledgments and no marking gaps.",
